  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ANGAU Memorial Hospital Redevelopment, Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ANGAU Memorial Hospital in Lae was redeveloped by Australia under the Australia-PNG Joint Understanding on Further Bilateral Cooperation on Health, Education and Law and Order (2013). Funding under this investment represents Australia&apos;s contribution. The Redevelopment of 21,000 m2 is a key investment for the PNG-Australia Partnership and the largest infrastructure project since PNG&#x2019;s independence and includes a new acute services building; maternal and newborn care facilities; family support centre; general and specialist wards; waste management and others. It aimed to position the hospital as a leading specialist healthcare provider for PNG. The investment included the construction work, and the wrap around support to make the new facilities function as effectively as possible. This included commissioning support; clinical upskilling and other professional development; support to the hospital management and Morobe Provincial Health Authority.</narrative>
  </description>
